Step 6: Retransmissions and the geometric distribution
The number of attempts until the first clean packet follows a geometric distribution because each retransmission is assumed to be an independent Bernoulli trial with a constant success probability 
. We are using the convention where the random variable counts the total number of attempts, meaning its support starts at 1, rather than the convention that counts failures before the first success (which starts at 0).

The closed-form formulas for the mean and variance under this convention (starting at 1) are:

